PURPOSE:
  This file mirrors the BUILT_IN_CORPUS placeholder in MLLM-5.2.py —
  define your autocomplete-based corpus here. Lightweight preview:
  no custom corpus included — simply a place to define your own
  autocomplete-based ghost-text examples (prefix → continuation).
  Ghost-text learns your style. Lightweight and local by design.

HOW TO USE — 2 steps:
  1) Edit: delete EXAMPLE block below, paste your text under PASTE line.
     Keep filename exactly "MLLM 5.2 preview" (spaces, no extension).
  2) Run:  python MLLM-5.2.py --corpus "MLLM 5.2 preview" "your prefix" --steps 16
  Ghost: type prefix → dim ghost-text → Tab to accept, Esc to dismiss.

FORMAT GUIDANCE — autocomplete-based corpus:
  - Plain UTF-8 text, one sentence per line ideal.
  - Each line is a ghost-text example: prefix → continuation.
  - Keep punctuation (. ! ?) — meaningful for generation.
  - Blank lines OK (treated as separators).
  - Size sweet spot: 5KB–500KB. Smaller fine for testing.
  - Tokenized lowercased as \b[a-zA-Z0-9']+\b|[.!?]

PRIVACY:
  Your corpus stays local, never uploaded. Training and generation
  happen fully on-device — nothing leaves your machine.

